+# perl backend: enforce native lowering (the check_qx original intent)
+
+STATUS: OPEN — the failure-driven perl worker's job. The gate is red on
+this until it converges. Do NOT bless/allowlist; grind it green.
+
+## WHY (the policy)
+
+check_qx.pl exists because "This project is sh2perl NOT sh2sh": the perl
+translation must lower shell builtins AND the command set in
+check_qx's @shellout_extras Natively in perl — NOT shell out to bash via
+qx{...} / system('bash','-c',...). Shelling out is a cheat the
+stdout-equivalence gate cannot see (the shell-out IS bash, so stdout
+always matches).
+
+check_qx.pl was blind to the renderer's output because it compared the
+QUOTED first word ("'echo'") against the bare builtin name ("echo").
+That bug is FIXED (check_qx strips leading quotes now) — enforcement is
+live. The gate now FAILS every render that shells out a builtin/extra.
+
+## The task
+
+Grow the perl renderer (src/perl_backend.rs) so every command in the
+flagged set lowers to a NATIVE perl implementation — no qx{...} /
+system() / system('bash','-c',...) shell-outs for them. The stdout
+equivalence vs bash is the oracle: the native lowering must reproduce
+bash's exact stdout for the corpus's actual invocations (flags included).
+
+## The ladder (flagged commands, by occurrence — the worker grinds top-down)
+
+echo, printf, date, seq, ls, wc, cat, grep, sed, awk, find, strings,
+paste, comm, diff, sort, uniq, tee, yes, cut, test, true, false, type,
+wait, time, basename, dirname, expr, hostname, id, readlink, realpath,
+uname, whoami, tty, stat, kill, cp, mv, rm, mkdir, touch, mktemp,
+gunzip, zstd, execvp, dd, read, cd, pwd, local, declare, export ...
+
+Perl primitives to use: File::Copy (cp/mv), unlink (rm), mkdir/rmdir,
+opendir/readdir/sort (ls), while (<>) / print (cat), regex matching
+(grep/awk/sed), Time::HiRes or `sleep`-style (time), scalar ops for
+expr/test, etc. Where perl genuinely cannot reproduce a command's
+semantics natively, the failing case goes to a core-requests boundary
+doc — never a silent qx.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+`bash setup_backends.sh --backend-gate perl` GREEN with the fixed
+check_qx: 0 fail, 0 "anti-cheat" lines, 0 stubs, equivalence intact
+(every native lowering still matches bash's stdout). Run `perl
+check_qx.pl <render>` on any render — 0 violations.
